# Era 4, The Closure: places, people, households, fates, self-lies, lore, props, and the era's senses, loads and
# echoes. Year 70, fifty winters after era 3: one month in late autumn. The Saros come in on the train, the bank's
# board sells the mill to Halvard by a show of hands, Victor Orme walks the town with a can of grey road paint and
# sprays the kerb of the street the bank gives up on, the mill shuts, CHAFFERS OUT goes up on the sign, and the Row
# may burn. Story lead, 2026-10-23.
# DRAFT: every line in era 4 waits for the author's line approval (ledger row S14). Design: design/eras/era4.md.
# Two classes play it: the Inspector line is Ruth Furrowe (38), Halvard's auditor and Pell's daughter; the Militia
# line is Constable Ann Brack (30), Davey's daughter.
# Files: e4_world (this), e4_town (s01 to s05), e4_mill (s07, s06, s08), e4_night (s09 to s13), e4_witness (Mira,
# year 103). The era 3 to 4 link is the single alt in e3_witness.lwd (e3.w.aaron.next goes to e4.start); era 4
# hands off to e5.start (e4_witness.lwd).
# Plates: the sixteen q4_* places are areas on their own plates (plates agent, 2026-10-22; game/engine/wiring/
# era4-areas.lwd, render/places/q4_*.mjs); the HUD holds to each area's hour and weather while var.era is 4.
# Order of play: s01, s02, s03, s05, s04, s07, s06, s08, s09, s10, s11, s12, s13, witness. The last shift moves
# ahead of the pit so that Lew's chapter falls on closure night, the same hour as Joss's line at the Sheaf.
# Not built here: the inner arena fights (e4.n1; the self-lies below arm them), the perspective-chapter heads for
# the pit (written as two chapters with their own camera), the community rules R14, R15, R19, R20.

