# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the fates, each with its decider
@fate f.e4_hire
pressure: has(e4.hire_open)
subject: household e4_saro
decider: JOSS
scene: e4.hire.decide, e4.hire.kasem, e4.hire.dale
window: 7
who: Kasem
because: the manager's order for agency hands a week before the gates shut; Joss Haldane gives the start to Kasem Saro at the agency rate, or to Dale Gedge at the old one

@fate f.e4_map
pressure: has(e4.board_sat)
subject: household e4_row
decider: VICTOR
scene: e4.map.decide, e4.map.row, e4.map.west
window: 7
who: Anzo
because: the bank's credit rule; Victor Orme walks the town with Halvard's can of grey road paint and sprays the kerb of one street more after Haldane Yard, the Row or Exchange Street west, and no credit goes to a street with the grey stripe

@fate f.e4_lew
pressure: has(e4.pit_open)
subject: household e4_lew
decider: COL
scene: e4.lew.decide, e4.lew.dies, e4.lew.lives
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Lew
because: the mill shut and the clinic with it; Col Haldane sells his cousin Lew the strip on closure night, or says not you

@fate f.e4_row
pressure: has(e4.row_marked)
subject: household e4_row
decider: DALE
scene: e4.row.decide, e4.row.burns, e4.row.stands
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Anzo
because: the poster, the pub and what the Sheaf did with Joss's words; Dale Gedge puts a bottle through a window on the Row, or paints the sign and goes home

@fate f.e4_shelter
pressure: has(e4.row_marked)
subject: household e4_saro
decider: ANNI
scene: e4.shelter.decide, e4.shelter.anni, e4.shelter.well
window: 7
who: Mira
because: the Row burnt or marked; Anni Haldane takes the Saros into Joss's flat over his objection, or they sleep on the Well House floor

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the self-lies (each echoed word for word in Mira's witness)
@selflie e4.sl.barn
about: COWARDICE, The Long Barn's return for Ruth, at the end of the Row on the walk with the can, the boy in the doorway in his hat (e4_town.lwd, e4.walk.ruth)
happened: The mill shut on a Friday. That night Lew Haldane died on stairwell C of the far-bank estate, on a strip from the clinic's last scripts. ? has(e4.lew_dead)
happened: The mill shut on a Friday, and the men stood in the yard after the last machine and nobody went home.

@selflie e4.sl.goats
about: DISGUST, Under the Goats' return for Ann as CHAFFERS OUT, on Exchange Street under the sign (e4_night.lwd, e4.sign.ann)
happened: The Row burned. Anzo Velek died on the pavement with his lungs full of the stairwell, and in the morning the sergeant stood in the black water in the hall and said electrical, and Ann said it after him. ? has(e4.anzo_dead)
happened: CHAFFERS OUT stayed on the sign through the winter. The Saros' front window on the Row was put through twice before Christmas.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- lore
@chain e4.map
name: The grey stripe
# the stripe already under Haldane Yard's arch, and the test squirt on the Row's kerb before the board sat
route: one-run | e4.lore.map, e4.lore.map_draft

@lore e4.lore.map
chain: e4.map
layer: surface
where: node e4.walk
about: The grey stripe across the cobbles under Haldane Yard's arch, sprayed the week before, scuffed by the school kids' heels and not coming off.

@lore e4.lore.map_draft
chain: e4.map
layer: deep
where: node e4.walk.ruth
where: node e4.walk.ann
about: A grey dot the size of a coin on the Row's kerb by the drain, dry by the time the walk comes down the hill: somebody tried the can there that morning, before the board sat down.

@chain e4.fire
name: The night of the sign
# the goat sprayed on the bank wall with the arrow down the hill, and who did it: Mrs Bora's hands, or the white on Ann's thumb
route: one-run | e4.lore.poster, e4.lore.witness
route: one-run | e4.lore.poster, e4.lore.pocketbook

@lore e4.lore.poster
chain: e4.fire
layer: surface
where: node e4.sign.street
about: Under the defaced sign, on the bank's wall, a white goat sprayed through a card stencil, head down, facing forward, with an arrow under it pointing down the hill to the Row. The paint is still running.

@lore e4.lore.witness
chain: e4.fire
layer: deep
where: node e4.report.ruth
where: node e4.report.ann
about: Mrs Bora from upstairs at number six, who cannot hear, takes the guest's wrist on the morning after and shows with her hands what she saw from her window: a man across the road, a ladder on his shoulder, whistling the mill song with no sound.

@lore e4.lore.pocketbook
chain: e4.fire
layer: hidden
where: node e4.report.desk
requires: class militia
about: The white still in the creases of Ann's thumb and first finger the morning after, from holding Dale Gedge's paint tin at the foot of his ladder. She rubs it with the other thumb at the desk, and it does not come off.

@chain e4.cage
name: The birdcage
# the cage on the platform, and what was left at the border: the seventh saucer laid on Anni's table and taken back
route: one-run | e4.lore.birdcage, e4.lore.border

@lore e4.lore.birdcage
chain: e4.cage
layer: surface
where: node e4.wide
about: An empty birdcage, brass gone brown, the door wired shut. Packed in the straw at the bottom, six tea glasses in their saucers, and a seventh saucer with no glass.

@lore e4.lore.border
chain: e4.cage
layer: deep
where: node e4.shelter.kitchen
about: Mira takes the tea glasses out of the birdcage's straw onto Anni's table, and then the seventh saucer, the one with no glass, and lays it with the others, and Kasem says a name, Aven, his brother's, left at the border, and she puts the saucer back in the straw.

@chain e4.carried
name: What was said on the Crown's steps, and in the Brack kitchen
# the carried words pass again: Pell to Ruth before the board, Davey to Ann before her shift
route: two-classes | e4.lore.carry_f, e4.lore.carry_b
route: one-run | e4.lore.carry_f
route: one-run | e4.lore.carry_b

@lore e4.lore.carry_f
chain: e4.carried
layer: deep
where: node e4.carry.pell
requires: class inspector
about: What Pell has from his father on the step after the Well House fire, and has not said in fifty years: I carried him. You don't need two for that. Will Brack's words, to Ned, on the Crown's steps.

@lore e4.lore.carry_b
chain: e4.carried
layer: deep
where: node e4.carry.davey
requires: class militia
about: What Davey has from his father in the Brack kitchen, the night of the Well House fire, with his feet in a bowl: I carried him. You don't need two for that.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- props (era4.md section 7, on their plates' marks; render/props/e4_*.mjs)
# The device rule (2026-10-23): no prop is a document. The map, the poster and the report became the can, the goat on
# the wall and the bottle neck in its bag; the ids stay so the plates and w_lore.lwd keep their hooks.
@prop q.bank_map
from: 4
name: The can of road paint
place: q4_board
mark: map
tells: era
carries: sound
touch: lift "Pick up the can" | Heavier than it looks, and cold. The ball inside knocks from end to end when you tip it. There's grey dried on the nozzle, and now on your finger. {sense: e4.can.rattle}
state: 4 easel | A spray can of grey road paint on the ledge of an empty easel, the kind the council's men use to ring a hole in the road. It has left a grey ring on the ledge.

@prop q.edrin_poster
from: 4
name: The end wall of the Row
place: q4_row
mark: poster
tells: era
carries: smell
touch: wipe "Wipe it with your sleeve" ? has(e4.sign_painted) | The white comes off on the cuff, wet, and leaves a smeared goat behind on the brick. The smell of it stays on your wrist. {sense: e4.paint.wet}
state: 4 wet ? has(e4.sign_painted) | A white goat on the end wall of the Row, sprayed through a card stencil, head down, facing forward. The paint is still wet and has run from its feet in thin lines to the pavement.
state: 4 bare | The end wall of the Row, black brick, with a pale square where an old bill was scraped off and the paste left on.

@prop q.fire_report
from: 4
name: The bag on the desk
place: q4_police
mark: report
tells: era
carries: smell
touch: smell "Smell the bag" ? has(e4.row_burned) | Petrol, through the plastic. Under it the rag. Under that, white paint. {sense: e4.petrol}
state: 4 typed ? has(e4.row_burned) | A police bag on the desk by the typewriter with the neck of a milk bottle in it, the rag still stuffed in the neck and burnt black at the end. Somebody has stood a mug of tea on it.
state: 4 brick | A police bag on the desk with half a red brick in it, and grit in the corners of the bag. Nobody has filled in the tag.

@prop q.tea_glass
from: 4
name: The tea glass
place: q4w_saro_flat
mark: tea_glass
tells: era
carries: heat
touch: hold "Hold the glass" | Hot through the brass holder, too hot at the rim, and the sugar not gone down yet. {sense: e4.glass.warm}
state: 4 poured | A tulip glass in a brass holder, sugar beside it. Mira pours for the guest first and watches until he drinks.

@prop q.orme_sign
from: 4
name: The board over the mill gate
place: q4_mill_yard
mark: gate_sign
tells: era
carries: sight
state: 4 painted | HALVARD in new white paint across the gate board. Under it, coming through, the old name in black.

