# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the era's loads
@load e4.load.cashbox
name: The cash box of pay envelopes
weight: 7
line: The cash box pulls your arm straight. The envelopes shift on their edges inside it when you walk.

@load e4.load.anzo
name: Anzo Velek
weight: 64
sense: e4.drag
line: He is heavier than he looks, and nothing in him helps.

@load e4.load.bag
name: A scorched bag off the Row
weight: 14
line: The bag smells of smoke and cloves. Something in it is hard, a pan or an iron, and it knocks your knee every step.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the echoes: what each fate leaves in a place the player comes back to
@echo e4.e.hire
place: q4_mill_yard
when: has(e4.dale_hired) & has(e4.closed)
from: 4
to: 4
tells: fate f.e4_hire
show: sound wind 0.25 near
line: On the fence wire by the side gate, where the line stood, a plastic bag has caught and gone white with the rain, the kind you keep papers dry in. It lifts when the wind comes over the yard.

@echo e4.e.map
place: q4_row
when: has(e4.map_row) & has(e4.sheaf_said)
from: 4
to: 4
tells: fate f.e4_map
show: light cold
line: The grey stripe along the Row's kerb has dried pale under the sodium, and there's the print of a child's shoe in it, from when it was wet.

@echo e4.e.map_west
place: q4_exchange_street
when: has(e4.map_west) & has(e4.sheaf_said)
from: 4
to: 4
tells: flag e4.map_west
line: Along the kerb at the top end, under the pear tree, the grey stripe, and lying on it a pear the wind brought down, gone soft.

@echo e4.e.dark
place: q4_row
when: has(e4.lights_out) & has(e4.sheaf_said)
from: 4
to: 4
tells: flag e4.lights_out
show: light dim
sense: room.cold
line: Number six has no light in it but a candle, going from room to room behind the curtains. At the downstairs window somebody's breath shows on the glass.

@echo e4.e.row
place: q4_row
when: has(e4.anzo_dead) & has(e4.report_filed)
from: 4
to: 4
tells: fate f.e4_row
show: sound drip 0.4 near
show: light cold
sense: room.burnt
line: Number six is black to the eaves. Water runs out under the door and down the whitened step in a thin grey stream, and inside something drips, slow, onto something hollow.

@echo e4.e.crosses
place: q4_row
when: has(e4.row_stood) & has(e4.report_filed)
from: 4
to: 4
tells: flag e4.row_stood
line: On every door on the Row there's a small white cross at the height of a man's eye, and on the step of number six the window glass, in pieces, that nobody has swept yet.

@echo e4.e.cage
place: q4w_saro_flat
when: has(e4.anzo_dead)
tells: fate f.e4_row
show: light warm
line: On the windowsill, where another family would keep a plant, the birdcage, the brass still black in its joints, and nothing in it.

@echo e4.e.brick
place: q4w_saro_flat
when: has(e4.row_stood)
tells: flag e4.row_stood
line: On the windowsill by the tea tray, half a red brick, on a crocheted mat so it won't mark the paint.

@echo e4.e.lew
place: q4_joss_flat
when: has(e4.lew_dead)
from: 4
to: 4
tells: fate f.e4_lew
show: seat chair empty
sense: chair.empty
line: In the passage the phone is off its hook, lying on the shelf where Joss put it down after the hospital rang, and nobody has put it back.

@echo e4.e.shelter
place: q4_joss_flat
when: has(e4.shelter_well)
from: 4
to: 4
tells: fate f.e4_shelter
line: The sugar bag is still out on the door table where Anni put it this morning, full, with the top folded down.
